  "bb:web_validation": {
    "checked": "2026-07-06",
    "verdict": "PASS",
    "defect": "readr/vroom default type-guessing silently mis-typed sparse columns in R/build.R (vroom() with no col_types). In variableGrouping.parquet, columns level_9, level_10, level_11 and the trailing unnamed column (vroom-named '...20') were guessed as logical and NA-collapsed to bool@null_fraction=1.0, destroying all their values. The same guessing also coerced numeric-looking columns (phs, study_version, variable_accession, variable_name) to double, silently NA-ing every non-numeric value (e.g. variable_name entries like 'SUBJID','CONSENT'; 549-581 rows per column).",
    "fix": "R/build.R vroom::vroom() call now passes col_types = cols(.default = col_character()) and guess_max = Inf, so all columns are read as character (empty -> NA, real strings preserved).",
    "recovered": {
      "variableGrouping.parquet": {
        "level_9": "4167 string values recovered (was bool all-null)",
        "level_10": "500 string values recovered (was bool all-null)",
        "level_11": "77 string values recovered (was bool all-null)",
        "...20": "16 string values recovered (trailing unnamed column, was bool all-null)",
        "phs": "549 non-numeric values recovered (was double)",
        "variable_accession": "581 non-numeric values recovered (was double)",
        "variable_name": "549 non-numeric values recovered (was double)",
        "study_version": "549 non-numeric values recovered (was double)"
      }
    },
    "regeneration": "Nix dev-shell broken on ws4 (nix-hdt 404) and vroom/arrow unavailable to system R (4.3.3), so brick parquet was regenerated with pyarrow/pandas faithfully replicating the corrected vroom semantics (tab sep, ISO-8859-1, quote='\"', escape_double, na=c('','NA'), trim_ws, name_repair='unique' -> '...N', trailing ragged footer rows dropped, all columns cast to string). Faithfulness verified against the pre-fix DVC-cached parquet: identical row counts, column names and all string-column values across all 6 tables; the only value differences are the intended recoveries above. R source fix committed for future Rscript rebuilds.",
    "note": "bb_validate.py reports null_fraction 0.0 for column '...20' due to a validator artifact (col.path_in_schema.split('.')[0] mangles the vroom '...N' name); the parquet itself correctly stores null_fraction 0.99996 (16 non-null of 424701). Data is correct; only the validator's summary field is affected."
  }
}